  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (RNA, multi-profile, PCA n2000, avgpool) is the current best at 0.591 accuracy, and the key findings are (a) multi-profile + avgpool strongly outperforms single-profile (0.591 vs 0.485) and transformer aggregation (0.591 vs 0.519), and (b) image-only is very weak (0.208). Uncertainty: We have only tested PCA as the RNA encoder. It is unclear whether a learned, biologically-informed representation (scvi) can capture structure that a linear 2000-dim PCA projection misses, or whether PCA already saturates the useful signal. This experiment (config_005: RNA, multi-profile, scvi_n200, avgpool) isolates exactly one variable — the RNA encoder — against the established best config_002, making the comparison clean and interpretable. If scvi_n200 improves on 0.591, it justifies further encoder exploration (scgpt) and multimodal experiments with learned encoders; if it does not, it tells us PCA is sufficient and we should pivot budget toward multimodal fusion or other levers. Under a limited budget, this single-variable test maximally reduces uncertainty about the representation design choice before committing to more complex multimodal configurations."
}

